# Make the backlight writable by the `video` group (session 70).
#
# WHY: /sys/class/backlight/backlight/brightness is created root:root 0644, so
# the desktop user (playbook, in `video`) cannot change the brightness and the
# bar's slider does nothing.  This is the same fix every phone distro ships.
#
# Install as /etc/udev/rules.d/90-playbook-backlight.rules, then
#   udevadm control --reload-rules && udevadm trigger --subsystem-match=backlight
#
# MEASURED (session 70) — this device's backlight is a *class device with no
# devnode*: `udevadm info -q all -p /sys/class/backlight/backlight` reports
# `E: SUBSYSTEM=backlight` and nothing else, **no `KERNEL=` property at all**.
# So a rule matching `KERNEL=="backlight"` never fires (that was the first
# attempt and it silently did nothing).  Match on SUBSYSTEM only, and use
# ATTR{} instead of a literal path.
SUBSYSTEM=="backlight", ACTION=="add", \
  RUN+="/bin/chgrp video /sys/class/backlight/%k/brightness", \
  RUN+="/bin/chmod 0664 /sys/class/backlight/%k/brightness"
